# Statement samples are byte-exact copies of a bank's export format, and the
# line ending is part of that format — Citi and Capital One ship LF, other
# exports ship CRLF, and parseCsv has to cope with both. Letting git normalise
# them on checkout would quietly delete the thing the fixture exists to pin
# down, on whichever machine has core.autocrlf set.
test/fixtures/*.csv -text

# A PDF is bytes, not lines: never normalised, never diffed or merged as text.
test/fixtures/*.pdf binary
